name attack-ccip-1
timeout 160

# THE CCIP DELIVERY, and the WHOLE pass: attack-ccrp.fbm's geometry flown on the other cue, and carried
# through the break turn and back onto the route instead of ending the instant the target falls over.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY DIFFERS BETWEEN THE TWO MODES HERE, and it is not the arithmetic. Both come out of ONE
# forward integration of the store's own ballistic table (core/FBBallistics) and the fire control
# publishes both cues on every tick. What differs is what the PILOT acts on:
#   CCRP  releases when the solution cue passes — the along-track countdown, and only that. A lateral
#         aiming error is the steering line's business, and a countdown cannot see one.
#   CCIP  releases at the same instant AND ONLY IF the predicted impact point is actually ON the target
#         (inside FBF16Pilot's AttackCcipTolM, 45 m — which is the Mk-82's own fragment radius against
#         this target class, so the gate means "a release from here would achieve something"). That is
#         the judgement a pilot makes with the pipper in view, and it is why CCIP is the VISUAL mode.
# So on a well-flown pass the two release within a tick of each other; on a badly-tracked one CCIP does
# not release at all and CCRP does. Both behaviours are the documented ones (doc/f16/weapons.md §2.5).
#
# `objective survive` is what carries the run past the kill: it can only be answered at the END of the
# run (core/FBMissionMonitor::Finalize), so the simulation keeps going through the whole egress — the
# 135-degree check turn with its climb, the 30 s hold, and the hand-back to the Route phase — instead of
# stopping one tick after the bunker falls over. SUCCESS at the timeout, exit 0, with both objectives met.
#
# Run the measurement with `--elev const` (see attack-ccrp.fbm's header for why).

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.80000  900 90.0 450       # due east at the target, co-track, 19 km out
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccip
  wp 46.90000 7.05000 900 450                # THE TARGET: the active steerpoint IS the aim point
  wp 46.95000 7.20000 3000 400               # the briefed route beyond it
  objective kill unit bunker
  objective survive                          # ...and come home able to fight: answered at the end

unit bunker
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 46.90000 7.05000 ground 90.0 0
